From e7fa64182dba19e5d69dd81a637ae181ebe0ed6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 06:46:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix program/workout creation, decimal weights and per-set
 notes

- Fix 500 on program creation: server now reads program name/description
  from form fields and parses programData as the exercise rows array
  (previously it expected a full object, so data.name was undefined).
- Fix the same latent bug in workout creation/editing (workoutData).
- Allow weights with one decimal place (e.g. 30.5) in the program form,
  workout form and live session; store as double precision (DB columns
  migrated via schema-sync; also applied to Neon directly).
- Add a per-set note field between RIR and the set-completion marker in
  the workout form and live session, persisted in exercise_sets.note.
